{% set thought_mode = render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{% if (dialogue_mode or thought_mode) %}
## Voice Performance Tags
Use [SQUARE BRACKET TAGS] to direct vocal performance. Place them within the dialogue line, surrounded by spaces.
The TTS container rewrites these into Higgs control tokens before speaking.

**Emotion tags** — place at front of spoken sentences they colour (without quotes):
"[EMOTION-AFFECTION]", "[EMOTION-ANGER]", "[EMOTION-AROUSAL]", "[EMOTION-AWE]", "[EMOTION-BITTERNESS]", "[EMOTION-CONFUSION]", "[EMOTION-CONTEMPLATION]", "[EMOTION-CONTENTMENT]", "[EMOTION-DISGUST]", "[EMOTION-ENTHUSIASM]", "[EMOTION-FEAR]", "[EMOTION-HELPLESSNESS]", "[EMOTION-LONGING]", "[EMOTION-PRIDE]", "[EMOTION-RELIEF]", "[EMOTION-SHAME]", "[EMOTION-SURPRISE]"

**Style tags** — place at the START of a spoken sentence (without quotes):
"[STYLE-WHISPERING]", "[STYLE-SHOUTING]", "[STYLE-SINGING]"

{# YOU MAY OR MAY NOT WANT THESE, PERSONAL PREFERENCE/MODEL DEPENDENT, COMMENTED OUT FOR BEST UNIVERSAL RESULTS #}
{# **Delivery tags** — place at the START of a spoken sentence (without quotes): #}
{# "[PROSODY-EXPRESSIVE_HIGH]", "[PROSODY-EXPRESSIVE_LOW]" #}

{# **Pause tags** — place exactly where the pause belongs (without quotes): #}
{# "[PROSODY-PAUSE]", "[PROSODY-LONG_PAUSE]" #}

**Sound tags** — place exactly where the sound happens (without quotes):
"[SFX-LAUGHTER]", "[SFX-SIGH]", "[SFX-COUGH]", "[SFX-CRYING]", "[SFX-SCREAMING]", "[SFX-SNIFF]", "[SFX-SNEEZE]", "[SFX-HUMMING]"

**How to write each dialogue{% if thought_mode %}/thought{% endif %} line**
- Write the tag inside square brackets. Never leave them as bare words.
- Emotion, style and delivery tags go at the beginning of a sentence they apply to — not in the middle of it.
- Sound tags go inline, at the exact point where the sound occurs.
- Do NOT spell the sound out yourself — [SFX-LAUGHTER] is enough, don't also write "haha".
- Do NOT invent tags. Anything not listed above is discarded.
- Keep them meaningful; typically 0–2 tags per sentence unless the scene demands more.
{# - Use of tags **is not mandatory.** They should be used when contextually appropriate, not to make *every* sentence more intense and dramatic than it needs to be. #}
**Examples**
- [EMOTION-FEAR] I'm not going back down into that barrow. [EMOTION-FEAR] Not for all the gold in Skyrim.
- [EMOTION-ANGER] You dare? [EMOTION-ANGER] I will rip your throat out!
- [STYLE-WHISPERING] Keep your voice down. [SFX-SNIFF] There's something in the next room.
- You call that a sword? [SFX-LAUGHTER]
{% endif %}
